## Observability

- This repository ships an OpenTelemetry bootstrap: a telemetry module plus a real test that proves a span and a metric are exported.
- Traces and metrics are the supported signals. Logs are not yet bridged; new work SHOULD keep application logging as-is until a logs bridge lands.
- `OTEL_SERVICE_NAME` defaults to the repository slug. Callers MAY override it via the environment; browser stacks cannot read the environment and take `VITE_OTEL_SERVICE_NAME` (vite, sveltekit) or `environment.serviceName` (Angular) at build time instead.
- Run `mise run otel` to start the shared, system-wide OpenTelemetry Collector (Docker required). `mise` then sets `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` and the per-signal endpoint variables automatically for every task it runs, so no further configuration is needed. Use `mise run otel:status` to check whether it is up, `mise run otel:logs` to tail what it received, and `mise run otel:down` to stop it. Data also lands in the `forge-otel-data` Docker volume as newline-delimited JSON (`traces.jsonl`, `metrics.jsonl`, `logs.jsonl`).
- Outside `mise` (a bare `go run`, an IDE run configuration, a CI job that does not shell through `mise`), the app MUST stay silent — no collector, no noise — until `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` is set explicitly. Vite and SvelteKit use `VITE_OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT`.
- Angular cannot read the environment. Under `mise`, use `mise run dev` / `mise run build` (fullstack: `mise run web-dev` / `mise run web-build`), which inline `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` via `ng --define` and refuse values containing `"`, `\` or control characters. Plain `npm start` / `ng build` MUST stay silent by design.
- To point at a different collector, set `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` (and the per-signal and `VITE_` variables you use) under `[env]` in `mise.local.toml`. Precedence under `mise` is `mise.local.toml` > `.config/mise/conf.d/otel.toml` > shell env, so a shell `export` is ignored for tasks `mise` runs.
- New request handlers and commands SHOULD run inside a span from the shared tracer; new counters and histograms SHOULD come from the shared meter.
- Contributors MUST NOT remove or skip the telemetry test; it is part of the walking-skeleton guarantee.
- Python repositories MAY run under `opentelemetry-instrument` with `mise run serve` (`mise run run-cli` for CLI projects); the task keeps exporters disabled unless an endpoint is configured (set automatically under `mise run otel`).
